This is the Flask Python project, and it uses the uv package manager. Its 
top-level directories place source code under `src/`, tests under `tests/`, 
documentation under `docs/`, and supplementary examples under `examples/`. The 
project runs tests with pytest and uses ruff as both its linter and formatter, 
so contributors should ensure their changes pass pytest and ruff. CI runs 
through GitHub Actions, though the specific workflow steps were not inspected. 
Because only uv was detected as the package manager, you should rely on uv for 
dependencies rather than assuming another tool like pip or poetry is the primary
workflow.

